  "body": "**Description:**\r\n\r\nInstead of using the rolling file handler, which does not do compresion, and leaves a gig of log files around, I suggest using a WatchedFileHandler\r\n\r\n```yaml\r\nhandlers:\r\n  file:\r\n    class: logging.handlers.WatchedFileHandler\r\n    formatter: precise\r\n    filename: /var/log/matrix-synapse/homeserver.log\r\n    filters: [context]\r\n    encoding: utf8\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis makes it easy to use with logrotate, which can provide compression and daily rotation, rather than log-size based rotation, which could result in all your logs vanishing in a day if something goes crazy. ",
